Imported Yul reports primitive-call arguments in source order.  The lower
expression language feeds EVM-like primitives in stack order.  This predicate is
the source-facing adapter between those conventions: the generated prelude is
still run in the source tower, but the final expression sequence produces the
reversed argument list.
-/
