/--
Checked root-dispatcher lowering target for the full imported-Yul theorem.

The contract dispatcher is lowered by `Stmt.toFunctionsList?` before functions
are lowered.  This predicate is the dispatcher-specific companion to
`CheckedBlockLoweringSound`, shaped exactly around the body equation obtained
from `Program.toObjects?`.  The future recursive theorem should prove this
from acceptedness/source fuel; public composition can then recover the actual
dispatcher body without exposing generated lowering evidence.
-/
def CheckedDispatcherLoweringSound (cfg : StateRelConfig) (layout : List Name)
    (terminalRel :
      Assembly.HaltKind → Word → State → Objects.Source.State → Prop)
    (revertRel : State → Objects.Source.State → Prop)
    (prim : Objects.Source.PrimitiveSemantics)
    (functionProgram : Functions.Program)
    (program : Program) (sourceFuel : Nat) :
    Prop :=
  ∀ {freshState'},
    Stmt.toFunctionsList?
        (Fresh.initial (Contract.names program.contract))
        program.contract.dispatcher =
      some (functionProgram.body.stmts, freshState') →
    SourceResultBlockSound cfg layout terminalRel revertRel prim
      functionProgram Functions.Source.Ctx.initial sourceFuel
      [program.contract.dispatcher] (some program.contract)
      functionProgram.body

/--
Run-filtered checked root-dispatcher lowering target.

This is the dispatcher-specific companion to
`CheckedStmtBlockLoweringSoundWhenFresh`.  It is still checked against the
actual lowering equation produced by `Program.toObjects?`, but its conclusion
is already shaped for the successful imported run.
-/
